<figcaption>On the catalogue&#x27;s own ratings, the cheap-and-hard-to-bias corner is empty: every process rated L or L–M on information cost is at most L–M to bias. Most hardening raises corruption cost by adding verification, which raises information cost too. The arrows are the moves the page names. The one drawn into the corner, composition, is unmeasured; the Hardening overview names deterrence as the likeliest family to get there. Cells are first-pass L/M/H judgments, not measurements.</figcaption></figure>
